From a42a89388589fccb60b14d641514992f0a74994a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adii14990adi-spec <adii14990adi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:24:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chore(animations): sync Unity metadata for the Mixamo FBX
 library

Adds the 74 authoritative `.fbx.meta` files from adii14990adi-spec/Animation-.meta- beside their exact-name FBX counterparts under unity-project/Assets/Animations/ (Combat, Crouch, Death, Movement, Weapon).

Adds processing/animation-metadata/sync_animation_meta.py, its 26 unit tests and sync-manifest.json so the copy is reproducible. The script:
  * matches by exact FBX file name and only writes beside a unique match;
  * hashes every .fbx before and after and fails if any changed;
  * preserves the committed GUID when the source importer settings change;
  * refuses to write when two assets share a GUID;
  * never overwrites metadata it did not create, and never reverts a local edit
    while the source file is unchanged;
  * is idempotent, and verifies its own output.

Adds .github/workflows/sync-animation-metadata.yml: workflow_dispatch plus a
daily poll of the public source, pre-flight GUID check, tests, apply, verify,
then a pull request on chore/sync-animation-metadata. It never pushes to main,
never force-pushes, never modifies an .fbx, and reuses an existing open PR.

No .fbx file is added, modified, renamed or deleted.
